A||||2||ChadMan||Bent mirrors||||5||
Z||000000||ChadMan||11-29-2000||10:36 AM||||My father-in-law has an 86 SE that is in great condition except for the passenger-side mirror - the first owner bumped her garage-door frame while putting the car away.  Not only is the pot-metal mirror cracked, it looks like the door itself is bent where the mirror attaches.<P>Does anyone have any tips on how to straighten the steel door where the mirror attaches without removing the plastic door skin?  Thanks in advance!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-29-2000||10:42 AM||||All I would have to say is get into the inside of the door by removing the door panel, and then you will also be able to remove the mirror.  Once in there you should be able to find how much damage has been done.  unless it is really really serious I dont think that you should have to remove the door skin.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-29-2000||09:11 PM||||This is tricky.<P>There is a spot you have to watch out for.<P>it's about where the front edge of the mirror base hits the door. It looks bent. It suposed to be that way. Don't straighten it or the mirror won't mount right and the top of the door won't line up.<P>You really want the out skin off for this. I've done this repair. It's not fun. If you try to do it with the skin on then odds are real good you'll slip and mess up the skin.<P>there's allot of notes on the doors in my cave.||||reg||1
